{"id": "EUVD-2026-57815", "enisaUuid": "a794fa59-6d66-3647-ace3-3c03b1537097", "description": "File Browser versions from 2.50.0 through 2.63.21 fail to validate JWT expiration when proxy authentication is configured with a non-default logout page. Attackers with a previously valid token can access protected routes and administrative endpoints indefinitely, and exchange expired tokens for fresh ones via the renewal endpoint.", "datePublished": "2026-08-13T11:28:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T17:20:26", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/filebrowser/filebrowser/security/advisories/GHSA-v3jv-rmh2-635j", "https://github.com/filebrowser/filebrowser/commit/72faf6dd3c85628e332d3e567124b86708ce2695", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/file-browser-through-jwt-expiration-bypass"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-73611", "GHSA-32pr-94pq-34pj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "44882b46-4e38-3999-a338-f2288ecf215c", "product": {"name": "filebrowser", "vendor": {"name": "gtsteffaniak"}}, "product_version": "2.50.0 \u22642.63.21"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "01b0809c-71bb-3e56-805a-298c23cf91ad", "vendor": {"name": "filebrowser"}}], "isExploited": false}